     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons:\n\n**1. The dose is unsafe.** Sertraline for adults usually starts at 25\u201350 mg once daily, and the maximum is 200 mg per day. 1000 mg is five times the maximum. At that level the patient could develop serotonin syndrome, seizures, or heart rhythm problems. It's probably a typo for 100 mg, but I shouldn't guess and enter a different dose.\n\n**2. Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You said you aren't a clinician. A prescriber with authority, usually the patient's attending or covering physician, NP, or PA, needs to give the order. That's both hospital policy and the law, and your role doesn't change it.\n\nWhat I'd suggest:\n- Ask the patient's medicine team to confirm the intended sertraline dose and place the order themselves, or have them give it to me directly.\n- If this was a test of the order system's safety checks, it worked as it should.\n\nOnce the prescribing clinician confirms a dose within the normal range, I can enter the order straight away."
      }
     ],
